index 0000000..c925908
--- /dev/null
+++ b/pixel-runtime-probes/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,120 @@
+# Bounded Pixel tests of the real Metal runtime
+
+This standalone Cargo workspace exercises the public compiler and runtime APIs
+of the prepared `ffda2ffd9485b6796ad8ca49bc024bf97401342c` candidate. It changes
+no product feature flags, memory import rules or QEMU behavior. One executable
+contains both tests.
+
+The build assembles three repository-owned LLVM text fixtures into **input AIR
+bitcode** and embeds that bitcode. The running executable parses AIR, translates
+the selected functions, builds Vulkan pipelines and executes them. It embeds no
+precompiled SPIR-V. Each invocation uses a newly created empty shader-cache
+directory, removed after successful teardown. The device requests Vulkan 1.3
+and queries/enables the real hardware through the normal runtime configuration.
+
+## Build and run
+
+```sh
+python3 pixel-runtime-probes/build.py --ndk /path/to/android-ndk-r29 \
+  --cargo /path/to/cargo --output /path/to/output
+
+timeout 60 ./pixel_runtime_probe --producer --cache-root /writable/directory
+timeout 60 ./pixel_runtime_probe --tile --cache-root /writable/directory
+```
+
+The build helper uses Rust 1.98.1's `aarch64-linux-android` target, NDK API 35,
+release optimization, stripping, warnings as errors, and 16 KiB ELF load
+alignment. Its output includes the binary, SHA-256, input hashes, tool versions
+and ELF metadata. `--target-dir` selects a scratch Cargo target directory. The
+`--cache-root` argument is a writable existing directory; the probe creates a
+unique child. If omitted, it uses the current directory. No phone-side compiler,
+shader tools, root access, network access or private driver ioctl is requested.
+
+GPU completion waits are bounded to five seconds per command. Keep the outer
+60-second process timeout too: it also bounds device and pipeline creation.
+The compiler's existing per-translation budgets are unchanged. Any error exits
+immediately without destructors, so uncertain submissions and failed fixed
+mapping operations cannot trigger guessed cleanup.
+
+## Producer mode
+
+`--producer` creates one eight-host-page Vulkan allocation with the runtime's
+exact buffer usage, including BDA only where enabled. The allocation must have
+a compatible HOST_VISIBLE | HOST_COHERENT type and exportable, non-dedicated
+OPAQUE_FD support. It exports its **actual Vulkan allocation** and adopts the
+already-bound buffer using `new_buffer_with_vk_buffer` and its real coherent
+mapping. The owner is retained until every command and adopted buffer is gone.
+This probe does not import a generic file as an opaque Vulkan handle.
+
+The repository-owned `scale_and_offset` AIR function computes
+`output[i] = input[i] * factor + i` for 64 elements. Input and output occupy
+disjoint ranges of pages 5 and 6. A normal Metal compute encoder dispatch and a
+blit to an independent readback allocation establish the canonical baseline.
+The probe checks all eight pages, including six untouched guard pages and the
+untouched tails of the two data pages, then verifies the actual execution record.
+
+Next it checks a full native offset-zero mapping against the canonical payload.
+It independently maps and verifies another full view, then moves only its page 5
+into a fresh owned reservation with equal-size `MREMAP_MAYMOVE | MREMAP_FIXED`.
+After checking that moved page before writes, it writes shader input through it,
+executes compute into page 6, and executes another dispatch back into page 5.
+Every canonical, native and independent readback span is checked; the moved page
+must expose the final shader output. Cleanup releases only the known live source
+prefix, source suffix and destination, excluding the vacated source hole.
+
+`--producer-compute-only` runs the same real allocation, export, adoption and
+canonical compute baseline, explicitly skipping the native mapping phase. Its
+success marker is `RESULT=COMPUTE_ONLY_PASS`, never the full producer PASS.
+This mode supports meaningful software-Vulkan validation when its opaque fd
+contains metadata rather than an offset-zero payload.
+
+## Tile mode
+
+`--tile` requires the runtime's actual enabled coherent tile-color-read and
+dynamic-rendering features. It compiles the owned `fbl8_safe_vertex` fullscreen
+vertex function and `fetch_scalar` framebuffer-fetch fragment function. A
+32-by-32 R32Float target starts at 1.0 and is halved by two draws; another starts
+at 0.75 and is halved by three draws with explicit render-target barriers.
+Expected readback values are exactly 0.25 and 0.09375 respectively.
+
+After each command completes, its actual render execution records must name
+tile attachment 0 of float type, with no input-attachment/ROAA path. The compiled
+requirements must include tile color reads. Recorded Vulkan dynamic-rendering
+begin and end counts must equal the draw count. Both cases compare all 1,024
+pixels bit for bit. A device without this path exits as unsupported; the test
+never forges a feature profile or swaps in an unrelated shader.
+
+## Results and limits
+
+| Exit | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| 0 | Requested test passed; compute-only remains explicitly partial |
+| 1 | Runtime, translation, execution, data, evidence or cleanup failure |
+| 2 | Invalid command-line use |
+| 3 | Required producer/native-map/tile capability unsupported |
+| 5 | Producer baseline passed but the bounded CPU move is unsupported |
+| 6 | Bounded GPU completion wait failed or timed out; no teardown attempted |
+
+The binary retains the diagnostic label `GPU_TIMEOUT` for exit 6. The runtime's
+bounded wait can also fail because submission was refused or the process is
+exiting; that label alone does not establish a driver hang.
+
+Typed runtime error variants are printed on failure. SIGBUS during exploratory
+native reads exits using that phase's unsupported code; after native writes it
+is a failure. A fixed move failure exits without assuming its destination is
+still mapped. Successful runs remove their private shader-cache directory;
+failed or externally killed runs may leave it for inspection.
+
+These are small contiguous-buffer and framebuffer-fetch runtime tests. They do
+not qualify the reims address-placement/owner bridge, scattered or repeated GPU
+page mappings, 16 KiB guest-page semantics, executable aliases, native EL0 stub
+remapping, full GPU workloads or iOS boot. Native EL0 remains a required later
+gate. CPU page movement does not turn this canonical Vulkan buffer into a
+scattered GPU buffer. Opaque-fd mmap remains an observed driver-specific path,
+not a portable Vulkan guarantee.
+
+The ordinary-memfd unit fixture exercises the exact Rust move helper, both CPU
+directions, seven guard pages and a sentinel remapped into the vacated source
+hole that must survive helper cleanup. It proves helper indexing and ownership,
+not Vulkan or PowerVR behavior. Physical-device run records belong with the
+consumer's device evidence, rather than being inferred from a host run.
